  "Question": "The lengths of segments AB and CD are compared by superposition: point A is made to coincide with point C, and rays AB and CD point in the same direction. Point B then lies in the interior of segment CD (without coinciding with point D). What is the relationship between AB and CD?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(AB>CD\\)",
    "B": "\\(AB<CD\\)",
    "C": "\\(AB=CD\\)",
    "D": "They cannot be compared."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Point B lies in the interior of segment CD, so AB is only part of CD. Therefore, \\(AB<CD\\).",
